{"data":[{"customdata":[["Human passengers and the human captain aboard the Axiom","Passenger leisure and minimal captain duties; rounded editorial estimate, not a census."],["Resident human-descended Solarians, including children denied full ruler status","Coarse editorial estimate of near-total release from routine productive duty; oversight remains possible."],["Immortal human bodies and their associated individual or joining minds","Narrative rest and automatic care suggest very low participation, while mental projects preclude certainty."],["Human residents of Two Rivers","Work is systematically displaced in the final town, rather than merely made optional."],["The country's human population, not an assumed uniform world population","Estimate anchored in the reported small productive core, reduced to allow useful voluntary activity among income recipients."],["Active conscious human residents undergoing private machine-generated dream experiences while their bodies are sustained in Comarre","Private conscious dream experience under automatic provision supports a high illustrative estimate; useful shared mental activity would count. Neither physical sleep duration nor unconscious bodies determine the rate."],["Harry Mudd, the resident living human receiving android service","Binary scenario for the one resident: assume Mudd performs no ongoing useful productive role while androids support him. If useful work is counted, the fraction becomes zero; this is not leisure time."],["Sara, the living human child in the hidden household","One-child hidden-household snapshot assumes Sara has no sustained assigned or useful productive role; ordinary learning alone is not work. Alternative zero applies if recurring farm\u002fhelp duties are assumed. Binary person counts, not time."],["Living human inhabitants of Chamocha","Explicit removal of work supports a high estimate, with broad allowance for useful human research and other activity; no canonical census."],["Living children raised in the implemented cradle system","The scoped residents are children receiving machine care without formal production roles. Allow a small amount of useful help; learning for their own development is not automatically labor for others."],["Living Thom; a deliberately narrow one-human beneficiary scope","Binary one-person scenario: no ongoing useful role is the central guess; useful activity would give zero."]],"error_x":{"array":[4.0000000000000036,19.999999999999996,29.999999999999996,8.999999999999996,19.999999999999996,29.000000000000004,100.0,100.0,25.0,19.999999999999996,100.0],"arrayminus":[1.0000000000000009,5.000000000000004,5.000000000000004,1.0000000000000009,4.0000000000000036,1.0000000000000009,0.0,0.0,5.000000000000004,5.000000000000004,0.0],"symmetric":false,"type":"data"},"hovertemplate":"%{y}\u003cbr\u003eЦентральная оценка: %{x:.0f}%\u003cbr\u003e%{customdata[0]}\u003cbr\u003e%{customdata[1]}\u003cextra\u003e\u003c\u002fextra\u003e","marker":{"color":"#277f75","size":9},"mode":"markers","x":[1.0000000000000009,5.000000000000004,5.000000000000004,1.0000000000000009,5.000000000000004,1.0000000000000009,0.0,0.0,5.000000000000004,5.000000000000004,0.0],"y":["WALL-E (Axiom before the return to Earth)","Foundation and Earth (Solaria after withdrawal)","The Last Question (Late humanity before final fusion with AC)","With Folded Hands (Two Rivers after the takeover)","Looking Backward from the Year 2000 (Reynolds's future America)","The Lion of Comarre (The sleeping city)","Star Trek — Mudd’s android-serviced captivity","Eden — Sara’s hidden robot-supported upbringing","Doraemon: The Tin Labyrinth — Chamocha before the revolt","Horizon Zero Dawn — ELEUTHIA’s first cradle generation","Beyond the Aquila Rift — Thom’s simulated sanctuary"],"type":"scatter"}],"layout":{"template":{"data":{"barpolar":[{"marker":{"line":{"color":"white","width":0.5},"pattern":{"fillmode":"overlay","size":10,"solidity":0.2}},"type":"barpolar"}],"bar":[{"error_x":{"col